If you get failed hunks it wasn't completely applied and that's the
reason it doesn't work.

And the version on Roderick Schertler's page is not only for 3.4.1 but
it also is a "patchable" version:
http://www.argon.org/~roderick/nethack/README.patchable

But if your version of NetHack is not prepared, such a patchable
version will fail.

I think you just have to do it by hand.

> Would someone point me in the direction of another patch that does the
> same thing?

I have the auto-open patch in UnNetHack. But I don't think the two
patches below would apply cleanly to vanilla NetHack, let alone apply
cleanly to a heavily patched version.

Patch: Auto open doors by Stefano Busti
http://sourceforge.net/apps/trac/unnethack/changeset/37

